[Desktop Entry]
Type=Application
Version=1.0
Name=Stella Scope
GenericName=Printer flight recorder
Comment=Record, rewind and inspect Stella (Klipper) - created by 3D3D
Exec=sh -c '"$HOME/.local/bin/stella-scope-launch.sh"'
Icon=stella-scope
Terminal=false
StartupNotify=true
# 2026-09-26: Stella opens in its own Brave profile with --class=StellaScope (a separate Brave process
# keeps the flag), so the class is its own; 127.0.0.1 also matched the 3D3D Studio window.
# Re-measured 2026-09-21 with wmctrl -lx on X11: the --app window reports "127.0.0.1.Brave-browser",
# so WM_CLASS is instance "127.0.0.1", class "Brave-browser". The old value "StellaScope" matched
# neither, which is why the taskbar showed no running dot. --class=StellaScope does not help: the
# launch hands off to the already-running Brave, which creates the window with its own defaults and
# drops the flag. Matching the instance name is what the shell can actually see.
StartupWMClass=Stella-desktop
Categories=Utility;Engineering;
Keywords=stella;voron;klipper;printer;3d3d;
